{"id":"f2f7f6c9-6579-4154-a050-459ac81e563a","expr":"args != null","rationale":"'args' is the parameter for main and is provided by the JVM; it should never be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Main#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Main.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:02.199058Z"}
{"id":"df5f12ed-0211-4c9d-9318-ae6d3fb29e53","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The entry point of a Java program ('main' method) expects a non-null array of command-line arguments as per the Java specification.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Main#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Main.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:02.199115Z"}
{"id":"f129eb64-c635-49a3-8547-ed642db1b47d","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"The length of an array in Java is always non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Main#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Main.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:02.199058Z"}
{"id":"cf0b6e7b-3318-4402-8656-065b6638c22f","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"Arrays in Java always have a non-negative length. Even if no arguments were provided, 'args.length' will be 0.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Main#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Main.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:02.199115Z"}
{"id":"2e9032bc-41d0-4fe3-9628-b0c6e2a5306f","expr":"name == null || name.length() >= 0","rationale":"Java's String.length() always returns a non-negative integer, so if name is not null, its length is at least 0.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Foo#bar(int,String):int","file":"com/example/Foo.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:02.671484Z"}
{"id":"6442f4f3-7840-43ce-8d70-026f4d3ef502","expr":"name != null || result == -1","rationale":"If name is null, bar returns -1. Otherwise, the result is something else.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Foo#bar(int,String):int","file":"com/example/Foo.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:03.728934Z"}
{"id":"7e1990dd-53f9-4720-89fa-42bfabe7f9bd","expr":"name == null || result == x + name.length()","rationale":"If name is not null, result is the sum of x and name.length() as per the method logic.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Foo#bar(int,String):int","file":"com/example/Foo.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:03.728934Z"}
{"id":"b77b8d76-9222-4341-a3ae-07946bb1d96e","expr":"result == -1 || result == x + name.length()","rationale":"The only valid return values are -1 (for null names) or x + name.length() (for non-null names), covering all cases.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Foo#bar(int,String):int","file":"com/example/Foo.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:03.728934Z"}
{"id":"d40dd1d6-99ad-416a-a3fd-14ea5eedc76a","expr":"result >= -1","rationale":"Since the only values returned are either -1 or x + name.length() (where name.length() >= 0), result cannot be less than -1.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Foo#bar(int,String):int","file":"com/example/Foo.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:03.728934Z"}
{"id":"7e457e3c-65f2-4643-b6a9-170c2537f130","expr":"name == null == (result == -1)","rationale":"The result is -1 if and only if name is null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Foo#bar(int,String):int","file":"com/example/Foo.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:03.728934Z"}
